      "writtenOn": "2021-09-28T22:42:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For TCPMv1 vs TCPMv2, I couldn\u0027t bring myself to intentionally break TCPMv1, so I added safe state there without adding the mux task support necessarily.  So it\u0027s just a little broken. \n\nFor adding safe state into the DPM, I\u0027ve actually convinced myself this should be okay for all boards, regardless of previous config functions, but cc\u0027d Tom in case we foresee something going wrong for trogdor.  We already have a safe state set in svdm_enter_dp_mode(), which is only overridden by an ITE EVB and kukui.  Evidently grunt used to override it as well to not set safe state, but got swept up in the USB consolidation a while back.  \n\nIt feels like this somewhat calls into question the exact timing of when we should set safe state (before entry or before DP config), but I\u0027m aiming to keep as much of our external-facing behavior as I can the same here.",
      "parentUuid": "0c31eda2_214ee20c",
      "revId": "85510b0fe07594091975f77b62af378d6323ee2f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
